{"request_sha256": "74fc185dfb393d6ce8569bdf62e51e1944c29ae999fed71b9edbc11f5773da28", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "be7e5b897bff8b7564caed3c86b0bc157c75f404f66604975e767d4170cc5399", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7541}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["rosette-crown-fronds (P-WHOLE, seed 1 and 42): the crown reads as a thin radial starburst of short, sparse, stick-like fronds, not a palm's rosette of long arching pinnate fronds; no frond descends below the crown base, so the drooping lower skirt of reference-0 is absent.", "owner-fronds-long-arching (both seeds): frond length is a small fraction of trunk length (crown spread roughly one fifth of tree height in render-0/render-1, against a crown spread several times the trunk width and frond length a large fraction of visible trunk in reference-0); leaflets render as tiny detached dashes along a bare rachis rather than dense stiff narrow leaflets, so the fronds remain far too thin and short.", "owner-trunk-straight-constant (both seeds): the trunk is not straight or gently leaning; it shows an S-shaped sinuosity with a distinct angular kink and a local diameter bulge near mid-height (clearest in render-0 and render-2), plus a pronounced continuous taper from a wide ground flare to a narrow apex, against the near-constant-diameter column of reference-1/reference-2.", "trunk-character (P-TRUNK, render-2): the trunk is drawn as a smooth untextured tapering cylinder; the diamond/rhomboid lattice of persistent leaf-base stubs and the reddish fibrous matting between them (trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern, trunk-fibrous-matting in reference-1/reference-2) are observably absent on a fully visible surface, not merely unresolved.", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no pendent fruiting bunches are present below the crown in render-0 or render-1, against reference-0; a core reference trait currently unmet (owner scopes it to fn-111, which is scope, not resolution).", "dead-frond-skirt and petiole-base-orange-sheath (secondary): absent in all renders; no brown collar of collapsed dead fronds and no rust-orange sheath material at the crown apex.", "Finish quality against the spruce anchor (anchor-0): leaflets read as hard-edged detached quads with black speckle and visible aliasing along each rachis, and the trunk is a flat near-black unshaded mass in render-2 and render-3; this sits below the anchor's even stochastic foliage and legible trunk shading. Finish only, no morphology weight."], "observations": ["render-3 (P-BASE, seed 1) is marked visibility hidden and the frame is filled by a near-black, featureless trunk wall spanning the image with only sky and ground at the margins; no leaf-base geometry, scale cue or ground contact is resolvable, so leaf-base-close is unassessable rather than absent.", "Both P-WHOLE seeds share the same crown and trunk character: seed 42 (render-1) is marginally straighter than seed 1 (render-0) but still carries the mid-height kink and diameter step; the deficit is systematic across seeds, not a seed outlier.", "The renders do satisfy the bare-trunk priority: no epiphytes, vines, branches or foliage occur anywhere on the trunk in render-0, render-1 or render-2. The epiphytic ferns of reference-1/reference-2 are scene features, not species character (inventory records them as variation), so their absence is correct.", "No crownshaft is drawn; the frond bases sit directly on the trunk, matching crown-shaft-absent in reference-1.", "The stem is single and unbranched in all renders, which matches half of solitary-columnar-stem; the near-constant-diameter half is not met.", "Foliage colour is a mid to deep green within the observed reference range (deep green in reference-0, grey-glaucous in reference-1/2), so colour is not a mismatch.", "Inventory statements were treated as attributed interpretations: trunk-lean-and-curve is recorded there as acceptable variation spanning straight to S-curved, but the render's curvature is an abrupt local kink with a diameter step rather than the smooth basal sweep of reference-0, and the owner's checklist is authoritative in ordering; it is therefore reported as a mismatch, not as variation.", "Relative progress over any earlier state is not assessed here and would not substitute for absolute support; every judgement above is against the reference-only inventory and the supplied photographs."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown in render-0 and render-1 is a flat radial spray of short thin fronds; the lowest fronds project outward and slightly down but none hangs below the crown base, and no frond arches. Reference-0 shows a rounded shuttlecock crown with many long recurved fronds and an abrupt drooping lower collar.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials sitting far below target, as the owner names; other causes (rachis stiffness curve, frond count) are equally consistent and none is established by the images."}, {"observation": "Leaflets appear as small isolated dashes spaced along an otherwise bare rachis, giving a bristly comb rather than the dense plumose V-sectioned frond of reference-0/reference-1/reference-2, where leaflets are inserted in groups at differing angles.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Trunk silhouette carries an S-curve with an angular kink and a local width step near mid-height, plus continuous taper from a flared base to a narrow apex, in all three trunk-bearing renders.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The host notes the taper dial currently sits at 1.0, outside its authored 0.05-0.6 range and outside the table; that is a plausible but unconfirmed correlate of the observed taper and is not required for the finding."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface is smooth and untextured over its full visible length; no leaf-base stubs, no spiral, no fibre.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The task states the trunk organs are not yet expressed by the generator (fn-110); that explains the state but does not resolve the trait."}, {"observation": "P-BASE render is a near-black featureless close-up of the trunk wall with the subject marked hidden; the leaf-base pattern cell cannot be read either way.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches below the crown in either whole view, against two to three orange-red bunches in reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Owner scopes the date cluster to fn-111; scope, not resolution."}, {"observation": "Trunk is entirely bare of growths in both whole views and the trunk view, satisfying the owner's third priority.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Single unbranched stem throughout, with fronds emerging directly from the apex and no crownshaft.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage green sits inside the inventory's recorded colour range; absence of trunk epiphytes matches reference-0 and is acceptable variation, not a mismatch.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Leaflet card edges, black speckle and trunk shading in render-2 and render-3 fall below the finish legibility of the shipped spruce anchor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "anchor-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Core. Render crowns are short, thin, straight radial sprays with no arching and no fronds descending below the crown base; reference-0 shows a rounded recurved crown with a drooping lower collar. Defining mismatch, not a finish difference."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. Leaflets read as sparse detached dashes on a bare rachis; the references show dense stiff narrow leaflets in groups at varying angles giving a plumose V-sectioned frond."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. The trunk is drawn smooth over a fully visible, well-framed length in render-2; the diamond lattice of leaf-base stubs is observably absent. Recorded as fail on what is drawn, not invented as present; the generator's deferral to fn-110 is scope, not resolution."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. No fibre or shredded husk anywhere on the rendered trunk surface."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core, partially met. Solitary and unbranched is supported in every render, but the trait specifies roughly constant diameter; the render shows a kinked profile with a mid-height width step and strong base-to-apex taper. The unmet half is defining, so the cell fails."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. No pendent bunches in either whole view where they would be plainly visible; absence is observed, not clipped. Owner defers to fn-111."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. No brown collar of collapsed dead fronds beneath the living crown."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation. Render green lies within the deep-green to grey-glaucous span the inventory records as an unresolved range."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. Crown apex shows no pale petioles or rust-orange sheath material; the frond bases meet the trunk as an untextured junction."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Inventory records this as variation spanning straight to S-curved. The render's curvature is not within that span: it is an abrupt local kink with a diameter discontinuity rather than reference-0's smooth swept lean, and the owner's checklist explicitly excludes waviness. Reported as a mismatch with grounds rather than accepted as variation."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Variation, and scene-dependent. Absence matches reference-0 and satisfies the owner's bare-trunk priority."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. Hue is a plausible mid to dark brown, but the trunk is rendered almost entirely in flat near-black shadow in render-2 and render-3, so weathering, stub-face lightening and tonal range cannot be assessed."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-3", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and marked uncertain in the inventory. A slight widening at ground contact is visible at small scale in render-0/render-1, but the dedicated base view is hidden and featureless, so the flare character cannot be confirmed."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. No smooth green crownshaft; fronds sit directly on the trunk as in reference-1."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the inventory itself. Proximal frond structure in the renders is below the resolution at which spine-like reduced leaflets could be distinguished from short leaflets."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Recorded as variation in the inventory, but the render falls outside the observed span rather than within it: crown spread is only a few trunk diameters and frond length is a small fraction of trunk length, against a crown several times the trunk width in reference-0/reference-1. This is the same deficit as the owner's first priority."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"1610fb12-8f77-4996-bad2-e80f1f2cd5c9","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator"],"plugins":[{"name":"flow-next","path":"/home/daniel/.claude-profiles/danithekiller93/plugins/cache/flow-next/flow-next/6.0.0","source":"flow-next@flow-next","version":"6.0.0"},{"name":"typesafe","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/typesafe-ai/typesafe/0.5.7","source":"typesafe@typesafe-ai","version":"0.5.7"},{"name":"firecrawl","path":"/home/daniel/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/firecrawl/1.0.9","source":"firecrawl@claude-plugins-official","version":"1.0.9"},{